Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 16:44:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03494/11362] [outer-loop] Q-head step 5: value routes L1 but
 does NOT deepen alone (level-specific gradient)

The crucial test: does the 7.6x-routing value reach L2 where blind fails? NO -- on ls20 + lp85 the
value reaches L1 efficiently (on=6, far=47) but neither it nor blind reaches L2 (exp=4000). The
value is trained on L1's steps-to-win gradient, so at the L1-complete state it has NO signal for
L2's different goal. The chicken-and-egg reasserts AT THE LEVEL BOUNDARY: to route L2 you need L2
data, which deepening can't provide.

THE VERIFIER-AS-Q-HEAD ARC (v1->v5): it is a REAL, strong PER-LEVEL efficiency tool (7.6x L1
routing, the session's first genuine positive, beating the linear head that "actively misled") but
NOT a one-shot deepener. The path to depth is the SELF-PLAY LOOP where the efficiency COMPOUNDS:
solve each level cheaply (learned value) -> spend the freed budget exploring from the level-complete
state -> find the next level -> train its value -> repeat. That iterated self-play deepening is the
real Phase-3 verifier-as-Q-head program; a single per-level value does not cross level boundaries.

verdict: complete: value_q_head_no_L2_deepening_honest_null_gap_sharpened

